cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this study, its data or its code, please cite it as below."
title: "Calibration Atlas: a reproducible calibration study of resolved Polymarket markets"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: Guinerve
repository-code: "https://github.com/Guinerve/calibration-atlas"
url: "https://guinerve.github.io/calibration-atlas/"
license: MIT
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-13
keywords:
  - prediction markets
  - calibration
  - forecasting
  - Polymarket
  - pre-registration
abstract: >-
  A calibration study of 11,881 resolved Polymarket markets from the 1,500 highest-volume
  closed events (January 2024 to October 2026), with event clustered recalibration slopes,
  Bayesian partial pooling across categories, a walk forward backtest of one trading strategy,
  and a pre-registered holdout test of the macro slope on markets that closed after collection.
